 "id": "water",
 "title": "Anomalous properties of water",
 "statement": {
  "text": "Water is a polar inorganic compound that is, at room temperature, a tasteless and odorless liquid, which is nearly colorless apart from an inherent hint of blue. It is by far the most studied chemical compound and is described as the \"universal solvent\" and the \"solvent of life\". It is the most abundant substance on the surface of Earth and the only common substance to exist as a solid, liquid, and gas on Earth's surface. It is also the third most abundant molecule in the universe.",
  "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Properties_of_water"
